WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.376
- It seems like you would be able

00:00:01.376 --> 00:00:03.096
to do the splits in just a few weeks

00:00:03.096 --> 00:00:05.534
but it's really not that simple.

00:00:05.534 --> 00:00:08.117
(upbeat music)

00:00:09.539 --> 00:00:12.899
- Full disclosure, I am
not very flexible at all.

00:00:12.899 --> 00:00:14.963
These are, like, skinny stretch jeans.

00:00:14.963 --> 00:00:17.162
I feel like I'm about
as stiff as they come.

00:00:17.162 --> 00:00:19.701
(grunting)

00:00:19.701 --> 00:00:22.004
This is about as far
as I can go right now.

00:00:22.004 --> 00:00:24.034
- I feel like flexible
people can save lives

00:00:24.034 --> 00:00:27.501
'cause they can, like, flexibly
move into little spaces.

00:00:27.501 --> 00:00:29.025
All right, this hurts right here.

00:00:29.025 --> 00:00:30.737
- I want to be able to do the splits

00:00:30.737 --> 00:00:33.820
because I want that flexibility back.

00:00:34.875 --> 00:00:37.387
(chuckles) Honestly, I think
this is as far as I can go.

00:00:37.387 --> 00:00:39.670
I wanna feel those muscles stretch.

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:40.715
(laughs)

00:00:40.715 --> 00:00:42.998
Oh, okay, no that hurts. Yup, right there.

00:00:42.998 --> 00:00:44.801
- My goal is to do better than this.

00:00:44.801 --> 00:00:47.718
And to actually hit this down here.

00:00:48.779 --> 00:00:49.984
- Each morning and each
night we're gonna be

00:00:49.984 --> 00:00:52.373
doing some stretches to
increase our flexibility

00:00:52.373 --> 00:00:53.622
so that at the end of this challenge--

00:00:53.622 --> 00:00:58.455
- I can do the dream splits
that I've always wanted to do.

00:00:59.861 --> 00:01:01.348
- Okay, guys, let's do some stretches.

00:01:01.348 --> 00:01:04.505
- We have to do ten minutes
of stretching every morning.

00:01:04.505 --> 00:01:06.702
- Today's the first day
where I'm going to try

00:01:06.702 --> 00:01:10.574
and use these bands so I can
learn how to do the splits.

00:01:10.574 --> 00:01:13.071
This smells so weird.

00:01:13.071 --> 00:01:15.962
- So I have to do a lunge, a leg stretch,

00:01:15.962 --> 00:01:17.777
a standing stretch, and
then try for the split.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.814
Slide your front foot forward, lean back,

00:01:19.814 --> 00:01:21.692
and slowly lower yourself to the ground.

00:01:21.692 --> 00:01:24.329
We're supposed to be doing
ten minutes of stretching.

00:01:24.329 --> 00:01:25.834
I'm trying to hold it, but
I'm gonna tell you what,

00:01:25.834 --> 00:01:26.773
it hurts a lot.

00:01:26.773 --> 00:01:28.326
- Stretching kind of hurts sometimes

00:01:28.326 --> 00:01:30.086
and they always tell you
in stretching videos,

00:01:30.086 --> 00:01:32.689
like, "Stretch into the
pain, breath into the pain."

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:35.106
Flexibility is hard, man. Uh!

00:01:36.336 --> 00:01:37.679
But sometimes you're
just, like, this pain...

00:01:37.679 --> 00:01:39.089
Feel the burn, breathe into it.

00:01:39.089 --> 00:01:41.649
...is, like, a lot and I
don't wanna do this anymore.

00:01:41.649 --> 00:01:43.820
- You can tell how out of shape I am

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:46.500
when, literally, just a stretch hurts.

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.673
A lot of spreading of the legs,

00:01:48.673 --> 00:01:50.406
a lot of bending over,

00:01:50.406 --> 00:01:52.378
a lot of putting your
legs on top of things.

00:01:52.378 --> 00:01:55.665
At first, it hurt a lot to stretch as much

00:01:55.665 --> 00:01:59.132
as it needed you to, for
like, every single morning

00:01:59.132 --> 00:02:01.254
but, the more and more I got into it,

00:02:01.254 --> 00:02:03.057
the better and easier it was.

00:02:03.057 --> 00:02:04.689
- One of the funny
stretches that I really like

00:02:04.689 --> 00:02:06.684
is, like, doing it up against the wall.

00:02:06.684 --> 00:02:09.553
And then you put your butt as
close to the wall as possible.

00:02:09.553 --> 00:02:11.371
Mom, are you proud of me?

00:02:11.371 --> 00:02:12.774
- I also went to Barre class.

00:02:12.774 --> 00:02:14.620
So you do the workout, you
do a stretch at the end,

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:18.470
and the stretch feels
incredible after a workout.

00:02:18.470 --> 00:02:20.854
I'm gonna go home and
I'm gonna see if I can do

00:02:20.854 --> 00:02:24.104
the split with my muscles super toasty.

00:02:27.244 --> 00:02:29.503
I can't go any farther. All right!

00:02:29.503 --> 00:02:31.935
We're supposed to be doing
a split in the next week

00:02:31.935 --> 00:02:35.685
and I still feel like
I barely made progress.

00:02:36.586 --> 00:02:39.161
- I think it's just,
like, kind of midway was

00:02:39.161 --> 00:02:41.932
a little bit of a mental
challenge and a mental hurdle.

00:02:41.932 --> 00:02:44.605
It's early and I'm supposed
to do these stretches,

00:02:44.605 --> 00:02:45.699
but I don't want to.

00:02:45.699 --> 00:02:46.532
But you gotta push through,

00:02:46.532 --> 00:02:48.517
you gotta make yourself
as flexible as possible.

00:02:48.517 --> 00:02:50.266
I don't wanna do the stretches.

00:02:50.266 --> 00:02:52.239
- Keep the post for 25 to 35 seconds,

00:02:52.239 --> 00:02:53.763
all the time focusing on your breathing.

00:02:53.763 --> 00:02:55.354
We have, like, one more
week and I've gotta be able

00:02:55.354 --> 00:02:56.826
to do that split in the next week.

00:02:56.826 --> 00:02:58.072
I imagine some day soon

00:02:58.072 --> 00:03:00.409
I'll be able to move my knee to my nose.

00:03:00.409 --> 00:03:02.915
- It feels good to stretch.

00:03:02.915 --> 00:03:03.887
There's something to it.

00:03:03.887 --> 00:03:06.702
I feel like I can touch my
toes a little bit easier now,

00:03:06.702 --> 00:03:07.917
which is a good sign.

00:03:07.917 --> 00:03:10.084
I used to not be able
to touch my toes at all.

00:03:10.084 --> 00:03:12.456
- These stretches, I
kind of did it as a way,

00:03:12.456 --> 00:03:14.451
almost like meditation,
so it was kind of, like,

00:03:14.451 --> 00:03:17.327
my morning wake up, kind of stretch.

00:03:17.327 --> 00:03:18.160
Send help.

00:03:19.444 --> 00:03:21.146
- My fiance was definitely
a little annoyed

00:03:21.146 --> 00:03:22.842
at my stretching because
I kept doing it while

00:03:22.842 --> 00:03:24.143
we were watching TV and I'd, like,

00:03:24.143 --> 00:03:26.950
kick my leg in front of the TV.

00:03:26.950 --> 00:03:28.091
Stretch.

00:03:28.091 --> 00:03:29.349
That was the best time to stretch for me!

00:03:29.349 --> 00:03:31.765
I might as well make
some use out of my time.

00:03:31.765 --> 00:03:35.162
- A big set back for me was an injury.

00:03:35.162 --> 00:03:36.378
I had a knee injury.

00:03:36.378 --> 00:03:37.989
I actually ran the New York City Marathon

00:03:37.989 --> 00:03:41.413
and halfway through the marathon
my knee kind of gave out.

00:03:41.413 --> 00:03:43.182
Mile 12, my knee hurts.

00:03:43.182 --> 00:03:46.697
And there's no one cheering,
and my knee hurts still.

00:03:46.697 --> 00:03:47.589
Geez!

00:03:47.589 --> 00:03:50.757
This is not exactly going
the way I wanted it to

00:03:50.757 --> 00:03:53.103
but I'm gonna finish this damn marathon.

00:03:53.103 --> 00:03:55.011
It was a little bit
painful for about a week

00:03:55.011 --> 00:03:57.242
but it also affected my
stretching for splits.

00:03:57.242 --> 00:03:59.610
My knees hurt really bad,
so I'm a have to ice 'em.

00:03:59.610 --> 00:04:02.181
If you have an injury
it's always good to, like,

00:04:02.181 --> 00:04:03.695
stretch it out, loosen it up,

00:04:03.695 --> 00:04:06.050
and kind of makes it heal quicker.

00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:07.194
- Okay, now, less pressure.

00:04:07.194 --> 00:04:09.795
Oh my God, I still got,
like, six inches to go down.

00:04:09.795 --> 00:04:10.894
- [Man] You're pretty close though.

00:04:10.894 --> 00:04:11.727
- You think so?

00:04:11.727 --> 00:04:12.810
- [Man] Yeah.

00:04:13.802 --> 00:04:16.666
- I definitely think I
became more flexible, yeah.

00:04:16.666 --> 00:04:19.034
I know I can reach my
toes a lot better now.

00:04:19.034 --> 00:04:20.805
- I think there's probably a 25% chance

00:04:20.805 --> 00:04:23.107
of success for me to do the split.

00:04:23.107 --> 00:04:24.920
- Maybe, like, the performance pressure

00:04:24.920 --> 00:04:26.920
will help me do a split.

00:04:28.037 --> 00:04:29.704
Oh! Where's that at?

00:04:30.547 --> 00:04:31.861
It's better already.

00:04:31.861 --> 00:04:34.165
The stretching I've done
has made me more flexible.

00:04:34.165 --> 00:04:36.188
I guess let's try that dream split

00:04:36.188 --> 00:04:40.032
that I've never been able
to do, ever, in my life.

00:04:40.032 --> 00:04:43.532
♪ Come on, let's do it ♪

00:04:43.532 --> 00:04:45.450
I think this just goes to show that

00:04:45.450 --> 00:04:47.615
I need to more fully commit to things.

00:04:47.615 --> 00:04:49.482
I think I should've been stretching more.

00:04:49.482 --> 00:04:51.061
- [Hal] Ready?

00:04:51.061 --> 00:04:52.004
(grunting)

00:04:52.004 --> 00:04:52.896
- [Woman] Oh my god!

00:04:52.896 --> 00:04:53.996
- [Hal] Yes!

00:04:53.996 --> 00:04:55.498
- [Woman] You did it!

00:04:55.498 --> 00:04:57.054
- Flexibility man!

00:04:57.054 --> 00:04:58.549
Feels good to improve by three inches.

00:04:58.549 --> 00:05:00.191
I wanna be lower to the ground

00:05:00.191 --> 00:05:02.314
and I want to have straighter legs.

00:05:02.314 --> 00:05:03.413
So that's what I'm going for.

00:05:03.413 --> 00:05:06.413
(grunting) Oh, God.

00:05:07.932 --> 00:05:09.167
That's about as low as I can go,

00:05:09.167 --> 00:05:11.620
but I feel strong and I feel better.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.625
- But I definitely think I can
at least push past this time.

00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:14.875
- [Woman] Yeah.

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:19.007
- 22? I kicked this thing's ass!

00:05:19.007 --> 00:05:21.126
I don't know about
doing the splits, still.

00:05:21.126 --> 00:05:22.608
Stretching over is a little bit different

00:05:22.608 --> 00:05:24.874
than, like, spreading your legs apart.

00:05:24.874 --> 00:05:26.122
Now I know the proper form.

00:05:26.122 --> 00:05:28.211
So you kind of have to go into a lunge

00:05:28.211 --> 00:05:30.602
and then slowly and
gradually make your way down,

00:05:30.602 --> 00:05:33.215
instead of just, like,
popping right into it.

00:05:33.215 --> 00:05:34.298
So let's try.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:38.602
(laughs)

00:05:38.602 --> 00:05:39.920
- [Woman] Oh my God! You, wow!

00:05:39.920 --> 00:05:42.452
- Wow! Yeah, I just surprised myself.

00:05:42.452 --> 00:05:46.452
(happy piano and guitar music)

00:05:49.385 --> 00:05:50.785
This feels so weird.

00:05:50.785 --> 00:05:54.725
(exhales) Oh, yeah. (laughs)

00:05:54.725 --> 00:05:57.284
It gave me the confidence
to feel a lot more flexible.

00:05:57.284 --> 00:05:58.960
Like, I can definitely do it.

00:05:58.960 --> 00:06:01.243
I can kick the face if I
really need to (chuckles).

00:06:01.243 --> 00:06:03.632
So I think that's the
best takeaway from this.

00:06:03.632 --> 00:06:06.534
- If you're trying to
do a split, be diligent.

00:06:06.534 --> 00:06:08.989
Like, you actually have
to do the stretches

00:06:08.989 --> 00:06:10.716
to gain some flexibility.

00:06:10.716 --> 00:06:12.539
- Seeing my progress, like, in numbers

00:06:12.539 --> 00:06:14.064
has helped me be, like,

00:06:14.064 --> 00:06:16.784
"You know what I think
I can actually do this."

00:06:16.784 --> 00:06:17.968
- If you're starting out from kind of an

00:06:17.968 --> 00:06:20.251
inflexible standpoint,
it'll probably take you,

00:06:20.251 --> 00:06:22.299
like, a good three or four months

00:06:22.299 --> 00:06:23.878
before you'll be able to do a split.

00:06:23.878 --> 00:06:25.166
But I do see improvement!

00:06:25.166 --> 00:06:28.304
- So stretching consistently
does make you more flexible.

00:06:28.304 --> 00:06:32.144
It's just about how consistent
you are with the stretching.

00:06:32.144 --> 00:06:34.075
- Yeah, check my social media.

00:06:34.075 --> 00:06:37.731
I'll post if I'm able to do a
split in the next few months.

00:06:37.731 --> 00:06:41.648
(happy piano and guitar music)

